# ── Model weights ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEMPORARY: the fp16 checkpoint IS committed (~56 MB) so a fresh clone can run the
# service with no extra download. This is a convenience for testing and demos, not a
# decision to keep — binaries bloat history permanently and cannot be removed later
# without rewriting it. To undo: restore `service/artifacts/` below, run
#   git rm --cached service/artifacts/model.pt
# and publish the weights as a GitHub Release asset instead.
# Build the committable copy with: python scripts/pack_weights.py
# The fp32 original is ~114 MB and GitHub hard-rejects any file over 100 MB, so
# it stays out. Same for exported ONNX, which is regenerated by the notebook.
service/artifacts/*
!service/artifacts/model.pt
!service/artifacts/config.json
service/*.onnx
service/artifacts/*.onnx

# generated training set (scripts/deduplicate.py); regenerate, do not commit
data/dedup/
